1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:09,768
Eighteen metres under a pyramid in Mexico, in a tunnel sealed for eighteen hundred years, archaeologists found pools of liquid silver.

2
00:00:09,768 --> 00:00:10,331
Mercury.

3
00:00:10,331 --> 00:00:14,133
And some people say it was the fuel for a power plant.

4
00:00:14,599 --> 00:00:17,632
A power plant, built by the ancient Americas.

5
00:00:17,632 --> 00:00:24,372
Shiny mica for insulation, mercury for conduction, and a city that knew something we have forgotten.

6
00:00:24,372 --> 00:00:26,866
You have probably seen the headlines.

7
00:00:27,333 --> 00:00:30,127
So tonight we do what an engineer would do.

8
00:00:30,127 --> 00:00:36,366
We write the parts list for this machine, and check every part against what was actually dug up.

9
00:00:36,833 --> 00:00:38,180
Part one, mercury.

10
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:39,303
Part two, mica.

11
00:00:39,303 --> 00:00:43,121
Then the wires, the power source, the signs of use.

12
00:00:43,121 --> 00:00:45,666
Each part gets a tick, or a cross.

13
00:00:46,133 --> 00:00:47,631
At the end, a verdict.

14
00:00:47,631 --> 00:00:49,945
Power plant, or sacred underworld?

15
00:00:49,945 --> 00:00:54,166
Let's start where the story starts, with a hole in the ground.

16
00:00:58,633 --> 00:00:59,333
Part one.

17
00:00:59,333 --> 00:00:59,955
Mercury.

18
00:00:59,955 --> 00:01:09,366
In the autumn of two thousand three, heavy rain hit the ruins of Teotihuacan, fifty kilometres north-east of Mexico City.

19
00:01:09,366 --> 00:01:14,500
In the great courtyard called the Ciudadela, the ground opened up.

20
00:01:14,966 --> 00:01:18,883
A small hole beside the Temple of the Feathered Serpent.

21
00:01:18,883 --> 00:01:24,337
The archaeologist Sergio Gómez tied a rope round his waist and was lowered in.

22
00:01:24,337 --> 00:01:29,233
He found a man-made tunnel, blocked in both directions by huge stones.

23
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:31,586
Ground radar showed the rest.

24
00:01:31,586 --> 00:01:38,806
A tunnel about one hundred and three metres long, running from the courtyard to the very centre of the pyramid.

25
00:01:38,806 --> 00:01:44,400
Its entrance had been sealed on purpose, with boulders, nearly eighteen centuries ago.

26
00:01:44,866 --> 00:01:49,771
From two thousand nine, his team dug it out by hand, a few feet a month.

27
00:01:49,771 --> 00:01:52,905
Spades first, then brushes, then toothbrushes.

28
00:01:52,905 --> 00:01:55,766
It took years, and the tunnel kept giving.

29
00:01:56,233 --> 00:01:58,638
Tens of thousands of offerings.

30
00:01:58,638 --> 00:01:59,647
Jade figures.

31
00:01:59,647 --> 00:02:02,596
Great conch shells from the Caribbean.

32
00:02:02,596 --> 00:02:03,605
Rubber balls.

33
00:02:03,605 --> 00:02:04,614
Jaguar bones.

34
00:02:04,614 --> 00:02:05,778
Wooden objects.

35
00:02:05,778 --> 00:02:07,563
Fifteen thousand seeds.

36
00:02:07,563 --> 00:02:10,899
Some counts reach seventy thousand objects.

37
00:02:11,366 --> 00:02:15,804
And the walls were dusted with ground pyrite, fool's gold.

38
00:02:15,804 --> 00:02:19,860
In torchlight, said Gómez, it glows like a night sky.

39
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:23,533
Forty feet underground, someone had built a sky.

40
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:32,336
At the far end the tunnel opened into three chambers, one of them cross-shaped, with two dark stone figures facing the wall.

41
00:02:32,336 --> 00:02:35,966
Robots with cameras went in first, to see what waited.

42
00:02:36,433 --> 00:02:46,255
Then, in April two thousand fifteen, Gómez told Reuters he had found large quantities of liquid mercury, in a chamber at the end.

43
00:02:46,255 --> 00:02:48,387
Rare in Mesoamerican graves.

44
00:02:48,387 --> 00:02:50,900
He called it a complete surprise.

45
00:02:51,366 --> 00:02:53,781
The headline went round the world.

46
00:02:53,781 --> 00:02:55,486
Mercury under a pyramid.

47
00:02:55,486 --> 00:02:58,470
Poisonous, silvery, impossible to explain.

48
00:02:58,470 --> 00:03:01,666
And a few years later, the story took a turn.

49
00:03:02,133 --> 00:03:04,137
But mercury is only part one.

50
00:03:04,137 --> 00:03:10,633
The second part of the story lies elsewhere in the same city, in the earth of another century.

51
00:03:11,099 --> 00:03:11,766
Part two.

52
00:03:11,766 --> 00:03:12,137
Mica.

53
00:03:12,137 --> 00:03:16,655
Mica is a mineral that splits into thin, clear, shiny sheets.

54
00:03:16,655 --> 00:03:25,099
In nineteen oh six, the architect Leopoldo Batres was restoring the Pyramid of the Sun for the Mexican government.

55
00:03:25,566 --> 00:03:29,338
He reported a layer of mica on top of the fifth level.

56
00:03:29,338 --> 00:03:30,386
And he sold it.

57
00:03:30,386 --> 00:03:34,437
The reports say the mica was removed because it had value.

58
00:03:34,437 --> 00:03:37,999
So that first discovery can never be checked again.

59
00:03:38,466 --> 00:03:40,976
Even the fifth level is a problem.

60
00:03:40,976 --> 00:03:45,773
Later studies suggest the Pyramid of the Sun originally had four.

61
00:03:45,773 --> 00:03:49,095
The fifth came from Batres's own restoration.

62
00:03:49,095 --> 00:03:52,933
The mica's context is a puzzle with a missing piece.

63
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,904
The second find is better recorded.

64
00:03:55,904 --> 00:04:05,922
In nineteen forty-two and forty-three, the archaeologist Pedro Armillas dug in the Viking Group, a compound south of the Pyramid of the Sun.

65
00:04:05,922 --> 00:04:09,500
It was named after the fund that paid for the dig.

66
00:04:09,966 --> 00:04:21,438
Under a mortar floor and twenty centimetres of gravel, he found two layers of mica sheets, each about six centimetres thick, with a thin layer of earth between them.

67
00:04:21,438 --> 00:04:23,733
The mica covered the whole patio.

68
00:04:24,199 --> 00:04:29,428
Armillas measured that patio at ten point four metres by two point eight.

69
00:04:29,428 --> 00:04:36,233
He dug test pits below, found no clue to a purpose, and stopped before he could try everything.

70
00:04:36,699 --> 00:04:39,374
Across the city, mica turns up again.

71
00:04:39,374 --> 00:04:41,181
Plates, triangles, discs.

72
00:04:41,181 --> 00:04:48,121
At the palace of Xalla, north of the pyramid, archaeologists found about thirty-seven kilograms.

73
00:04:48,121 --> 00:04:54,699
Together, these two compounds hold more than ninety percent of all the mica in Teotihuacan.

74
00:04:55,166 --> 00:04:59,325
In neighbourhood centres like Teopancazco, only grams.

75
00:04:59,325 --> 00:05:01,713
Mica was a luxury of the elite.

76
00:05:01,713 --> 00:05:08,491
It sat as discs on incense burners, as shining eyes in sculptures, as cladding on walls.

77
00:05:08,491 --> 00:05:11,033
Mica was jewellery for buildings.

78
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:14,885
So we have two real finds, one century apart.

79
00:05:14,885 --> 00:05:16,992
A silver liquid in a tunnel.

80
00:05:16,992 --> 00:05:19,023
Shiny sheets under a floor.

81
00:05:19,023 --> 00:05:22,033
Now: who first said they were a machine?

82
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:30,357
In nineteen ninety-five, Graham Hancock's bestseller Fingerprints of the Gods described the Viking Group mica.

83
00:05:30,357 --> 00:05:32,000
He called it a mystery.

84
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:37,500
He noted that mica is a modern insulator, used in capacitors and electronics.

85
00:05:37,966 --> 00:05:43,751
He wrote that the mica was a type found only in Brazil, two thousand miles away.

86
00:05:43,751 --> 00:05:47,078
That it lay in two sheets, ninety feet square.

87
00:05:47,078 --> 00:05:50,766
And he asked why anyone would bury it out of sight.

88
00:05:51,233 --> 00:05:53,566
Then came two thousand fifteen.

89
00:05:53,566 --> 00:05:58,986
Mercury was found at Teotihuacan, and the internet put the two together.

90
00:05:58,986 --> 00:06:01,696
Insulation, plus a liquid conductor.

91
00:06:01,696 --> 00:06:02,976
Mica and mercury.

92
00:06:02,976 --> 00:06:04,933
It sounded like a circuit.

93
00:06:05,399 --> 00:06:13,915
By twenty twenty-five, tabloids were calling the tunnel a gateway to the underworld that hints at an advanced civilisation.

94
00:06:13,915 --> 00:06:18,899
Blogs went further: an energy-generating device, an ancient power plant.

95
00:06:19,366 --> 00:06:20,830
Notice what changed.

96
00:06:20,830 --> 00:06:22,806
The excavators said ritual.

97
00:06:22,806 --> 00:06:24,782
The headlines said machine.

98
00:06:24,782 --> 00:06:32,833
And the only link between the two stories is a modern fact: that today, we use mica and mercury in technology.

99
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:36,059
That is not evidence from Teotihuacan.

100
00:06:36,059 --> 00:06:37,657
That is a resemblance.

101
00:06:37,657 --> 00:06:41,652
So let's test the three numbers people repeat the most.

102
00:06:41,652 --> 00:06:44,266
First: where did the mica come from?

103
00:06:44,733 --> 00:06:47,379
Tests on the mica itself have been done.

104
00:06:47,379 --> 00:06:49,033
The answer is not Brazil.

105
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:55,880
In two thousand seventeen, a team led by Linda Manzanilla published the analysis.

106
00:06:55,880 --> 00:07:00,528
X-ray diffraction, electron microscopy, neutron activation.

107
00:07:00,528 --> 00:07:07,933
Teotihuacan's mica matches the Central Valleys of Oaxaca, around four hundred kilometres away.

108
00:07:08,399 --> 00:07:16,904
Later work matched mica from the Viking Group to a huge stockpile at Monte Albán, the Zapotec capital in Oaxaca.

109
00:07:16,904 --> 00:07:23,814
There, a single area of the North Platform held about one hundred and fifty-four kilograms.

110
00:07:23,814 --> 00:07:25,333
Brazil: crossed off.

111
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:26,907
Next, the size.

112
00:07:26,907 --> 00:07:32,816
Ninety feet square would be about seven hundred and fifty square metres of mica.

113
00:07:32,816 --> 00:07:39,537
Armillas, who dug it, measured the whole patio at ten point four by two point eight metres.

114
00:07:39,537 --> 00:07:40,866
Size: crossed off.

115
00:07:41,333 --> 00:07:43,046
Now the real parts list.

116
00:07:43,046 --> 00:07:45,116
What does a power plant need?

117
00:07:45,116 --> 00:07:46,472
A source of energy.

118
00:07:46,472 --> 00:07:48,328
Conductors, usually wires.

119
00:07:48,328 --> 00:07:49,898
A circuit that closes.

120
00:07:49,898 --> 00:07:52,039
Something that uses the power.

121
00:07:52,039 --> 00:07:54,466
And, after years of running, wear.

122
00:07:54,933 --> 00:07:56,301
Mica does insulate.

123
00:07:56,301 --> 00:08:01,992
Early capacitors used it, with metal foil plates and wires to carry the charge.

124
00:08:01,992 --> 00:08:03,865
But mica alone is a sheet.

125
00:08:03,865 --> 00:08:06,242
It needs metal plates, and leads.

126
00:08:06,242 --> 00:08:09,699
Nothing like that was found in the Viking Group.

127
00:08:10,166 --> 00:08:11,264
And the mercury?

128
00:08:11,264 --> 00:08:12,155
Reports vary.

129
00:08:12,155 --> 00:08:15,105
Fifty grams, which would fit in a teaspoon.

130
00:08:15,105 --> 00:08:18,534
About two hundred millilitres, in another account.

131
00:08:18,534 --> 00:08:21,072
About four hundred grams, in a third.

132
00:08:21,072 --> 00:08:24,433
Not enough to power a city, however you count it.

133
00:08:24,899 --> 00:08:26,390
Next: any apparatus?

134
00:08:26,390 --> 00:08:33,770
No wires, no electrodes, no turbines, no tanks, no pipes, no burn marks, no residue: none reported.

135
00:08:33,770 --> 00:08:38,541
The mercury was found as drops, when soil was sieved and washed.

136
00:08:38,541 --> 00:08:41,299
It was in the earth, among offerings.

137
00:08:41,766 --> 00:08:44,423
A real power plant leaves a footprint.

138
00:08:44,423 --> 00:08:48,688
A source of heat or flow, fuel, ash, repairs, a wear pattern.

139
00:08:48,688 --> 00:08:51,344
Nothing in the tunnel looks like that.

140
00:08:51,344 --> 00:08:55,400
It looks like a place where things were put down and left.

141
00:08:55,866 --> 00:08:59,314
In fact, the tunnel is full of fragile things.

142
00:08:59,314 --> 00:08:59,689
Wood.

143
00:08:59,689 --> 00:09:00,139
Seeds.

144
00:09:00,139 --> 00:09:00,513
Skin.

145
00:09:00,513 --> 00:09:04,711
A jar with eighteen-hundred-year-old corn at the bottom.

146
00:09:04,711 --> 00:09:10,033
A sealed room designed to hold offerings is a poor place for a machine.

147
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:13,223
Even the mercury works against the theory.

148
00:09:13,223 --> 00:09:15,297
It is toxic, and hard to handle.

149
00:09:15,297 --> 00:09:17,567
It was never plugged into anything.

150
00:09:17,567 --> 00:09:22,299
It was put in, in small amounts, and then the tunnel was closed for good.

151
00:09:22,766 --> 00:09:25,134
Two ticks: the materials are real.

152
00:09:25,134 --> 00:09:27,642
The rest of the parts list is blank.

153
00:09:27,642 --> 00:09:30,359
But if it is not a machine, what is it?

154
00:09:30,359 --> 00:09:32,866
Archaeologists have a better answer.

155
00:09:33,333 --> 00:09:34,735
The ritual reading.

156
00:09:34,735 --> 00:09:38,572
Gómez's idea: the tunnel is a map of the underworld.

157
00:09:38,572 --> 00:09:43,515
A dark cave, a place of creation, where the dead and the gods live.

158
00:09:43,515 --> 00:09:47,500
And in Mesoamerican belief, that underworld has water.

159
00:09:47,966 --> 00:09:49,755
The pyramid above fits it.

160
00:09:49,755 --> 00:09:54,779
The Feathered Serpent temple is covered in snake heads, shells and waves.

161
00:09:54,779 --> 00:10:01,866
Scholars like Michael Coe and Clemency Coggins read it as the creation of the world from a watery void.

162
00:10:02,333 --> 00:10:04,960
So the tunnel below could be that void.

163
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:06,981
Pyrite on the walls for stars.

164
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:09,810
Mercury on the floor for lakes and rivers.

165
00:10:09,810 --> 00:10:15,200
In flickering light, the mercury would reflect those stars, like water at night.

166
00:10:15,666 --> 00:10:20,411
And Teotihuacan already loved the mercury family of materials.

167
00:10:20,411 --> 00:10:27,453
Cinnabar, the red mercury ore, was ground into pigment for murals and sprinkled over graves.

168
00:10:27,453 --> 00:10:31,433
Liquid mercury is the same element, in a rarer form.

169
00:10:31,899 --> 00:10:33,978
It is rare, but not unique.

170
00:10:33,978 --> 00:10:40,982
At the Maya city of Lamanai in Belize, a cache held about one hundred and thirty-two grams.

171
00:10:40,982 --> 00:10:45,600
At Copán in Honduras, around four to six kilograms in total.

172
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:49,833
At Kaminaljuyú in Guatemala, a burial had a small pool.

173
00:10:50,299 --> 00:10:54,251
Even more telling: the elite loved reflective things.

174
00:10:54,251 --> 00:10:55,369
Pyrite mirrors.

175
00:10:55,369 --> 00:10:56,637
Obsidian mirrors.

176
00:10:56,637 --> 00:10:59,023
Mica discs inlaid in sculptures.

177
00:10:59,023 --> 00:11:02,899
Shine meant power, and a doorway to the other world.

178
00:11:03,366 --> 00:11:04,036
And mica?

179
00:11:04,036 --> 00:11:11,707
The Monte Albán stockpile and the pattern at Teotihuacan point to controlled stores of a prized import.

180
00:11:11,707 --> 00:11:18,633
A rare, shining raw material moved by the rulers, then laid down in the places that mattered.

181
00:11:19,100 --> 00:11:21,649
A floor of mica under a patio is odd.

182
00:11:21,649 --> 00:11:26,473
But the Viking Group is an elite compound, and so is the Xalla palace.

183
00:11:26,473 --> 00:11:29,160
They are not clues to a hidden machine.

184
00:11:29,160 --> 00:11:34,466
They are signs of who held the luxury, and of what they were willing to bury.

185
00:11:34,933 --> 00:11:44,391
So the ritual reading has a reason for each part: a map of the underworld, water from mercury, stars from pyrite, shine from mica.

186
00:11:44,391 --> 00:11:45,192
Not proven.

187
00:11:45,192 --> 00:11:49,266
But it explains every piece without inventing a machine.

188
00:11:49,733 --> 00:11:51,041
But honesty matters.

189
00:11:51,041 --> 00:11:53,396
There is plenty we still don't know.

190
00:11:53,396 --> 00:12:01,833
Only about ten percent of the tunnel's offerings had been catalogued, when Gómez spoke to Smithsonian magazine in twenty sixteen.

191
00:12:02,299 --> 00:12:04,644
The amount of mercury is unclear.

192
00:12:04,644 --> 00:12:06,207
The source is unknown.

193
00:12:06,207 --> 00:12:09,973
A proper isotope study could show where it came from.

194
00:12:09,973 --> 00:12:13,171
A full inventory could say how it was placed.

195
00:12:13,171 --> 00:12:15,799
That is how you settle it, with data.

196
00:12:16,266 --> 00:12:22,084
Three sub-chambers beneath the end of the tunnel were still waiting to be excavated.

197
00:12:22,084 --> 00:12:24,439
Some hope for the tomb of a ruler.

198
00:12:24,439 --> 00:12:26,655
Others say the tomb is symbolic.

199
00:12:26,655 --> 00:12:29,633
Nobody knows until the last soil is lifted.

200
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:33,050
And the Pyramid of the Sun's mica is gone.

201
00:12:33,050 --> 00:12:34,174
Reportedly sold.

202
00:12:34,174 --> 00:12:38,950
Under the Viking Group, Armillas stopped digging before he finished.

203
00:12:38,950 --> 00:12:42,743
If a machine part exists, that is where it would hide.

204
00:12:42,743 --> 00:12:44,499
No evidence says it does.

205
00:12:44,966 --> 00:12:48,109
This is where the believers have a fair point.

206
00:12:48,109 --> 00:12:50,432
Not about aliens, or power plants.

207
00:12:50,432 --> 00:12:55,283
About the fact that Teotihuacan still hides far more than it has shown.

208
00:12:55,283 --> 00:13:00,066
We do not know the language, the rulers, or the real name of the city.

209
00:13:00,533 --> 00:13:02,396
But a gap is not a machine.

210
00:13:02,396 --> 00:13:07,570
A mystery does not become a power plant just because we lack the paperwork.

211
00:13:07,570 --> 00:13:10,951
The question is whether anything points that way.

212
00:13:10,951 --> 00:13:12,399
So far, nothing does.

213
00:13:12,866 --> 00:13:14,500
It is time for the debrief.

214
00:13:14,966 --> 00:13:16,239
Parts list complete.

215
00:13:16,239 --> 00:13:19,166
One last look at the evidence, and the theory.

216
00:13:19,633 --> 00:13:20,141
Debrief.

217
00:13:20,141 --> 00:13:21,666
Time to score the claim.

218
00:13:22,133 --> 00:13:27,226
Liquid mercury in a sealed tunnel, around the third century: evidence.

219
00:13:27,226 --> 00:13:30,936
Mica layers under the Viking Group floor: evidence.

220
00:13:30,936 --> 00:13:34,428
Mica from Brazil: debunked, it came from Oaxaca.

221
00:13:34,428 --> 00:13:38,066
Ninety feet square: debunked, ten by three metres.

222
00:13:38,533 --> 00:13:41,734
Wires, circuits, any apparatus: none found.

223
00:13:41,734 --> 00:13:45,009
A power plant or energy device: no evidence.

224
00:13:45,009 --> 00:13:51,933
An underworld ritual offering: likely, though the exact purpose of the mercury is still open.

225
00:13:52,399 --> 00:13:53,200
The verdict.

226
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:54,399
Not a power plant.

227
00:13:54,399 --> 00:13:58,466
The mercury and the mica are real, rare, and probably sacred.

228
00:13:58,466 --> 00:14:03,799
They were treasures laid in the dark for the underworld, not parts in a circuit.

229
00:14:03,799 --> 00:14:06,399
But the tunnel is not finished talking.

230
00:14:06,866 --> 00:14:13,171
Eighteen centuries ago, someone carried a silver liquid and shiny stone down into the dark.

231
00:14:13,171 --> 00:14:15,041
Not to switch something on.

232
00:14:15,041 --> 00:14:18,644
To honour the stars, and the water, below the world.

233
00:14:18,644 --> 00:14:21,000
That is already a wonderful story.

234
00:14:21,466 --> 00:14:27,717
Next case: a valley in Norway where mysterious glowing balls have drifted for decades.

235
00:14:27,717 --> 00:14:30,988
Are they plasma, UFOs, or something stranger?

236
00:14:30,988 --> 00:14:32,733
We put them to the test.

237
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:36,604
Do you think the mercury was water for the underworld?

238
00:14:36,604 --> 00:14:41,899
Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next ancient mystery put to the test.
